The five programming environments the brief asks for all need the same four
things from the engine, so they go in first, before any of them exists:

  · dependencyIndex.ts — every "reads from" relationship, typed: reader →
    read, with the edge's kind and field path, over questions, display
    rules, skips, calculations, quotas, named expressions, list fills and
    conditional flow containers. reach() and affects() are the two
    traversals; neighbours() groups them the way an inspector shows them.
    dependencies.ts stays as the runtime's lossy question graph; a test
    checks the two agree on every question→question edge.

  · objectStatus.ts — runQualityCheck's issues regrouped by OBJECT rather
    than by area, so a status dot can sit on Q14, on a flow node, on a
    named rule. LogicIssue gains an optional objectKey; runQualityCheck
    stops dropping FlowStructureIssue.nodeId and keys dead display rules.
    A duplicate variable lands on BOTH questions that write it.

  · questionOps.ts — add / duplicate / remove / move, once, as engine
    functions. QuestionsPanel's inline closures now call them (id generator
    passed in, so browser tests see the same ids). Behaviour pinned by 13
    tests before the panel was touched.

  · scale.ts — a 600-question fixture with tracker-like logic density, and
    a perf harness with budgets. Building it found that lintSurveyLogic was
    CUBIC in the question count (orderIndex recomputed per question, and
    questionOrder's includes() on top): 70 ms at 160 questions, 5.5 s at
    1 000. Now linear: 24 ms → 84 ms. A ratio test pins the curve's shape.

Also fixed: conditionSummary rendered a multi-child NOT as "not (A and B)",
which is NAND; the evaluator and formatCondition treat it as NOR. The Logic
panel and every Flow edge label read that string, so a programmer checking
routing was told the opposite of what respondents get. Now "none of (A or B)".

Every fix has a regression test and every test was mutation-checked.
docs/MULTI-MODAL-PROGRAMMING-PLAN.md holds the §19 audit and the plan.

